<<<
+ finding. The right solution is to start the sentence with And women are finding employment not merely &e. In Inversion the section headed inversion in parallel clauses is devoted to this & similar types.
===
+ *finding.* The right solution is to start the sentence with *And women are finding employment not merely* &c. In ^^INVERSION^^ the section headed *inversion in parallel clauses* is devoted to this & similar types.
>>>

<<<
3. Dependent & independent. The municipality charged itself with the purchase of these articles in wholesale quantities, & it was to the Town Hall that poor people applied for them, & were served by municipal employees.
===
**3. Dependent & independent.** *The municipality charged itself with the purchase of these articles in wholesale quantities, & it was to the Town Hall that poor people applied for them, & were served by municipal employees.*
>>>

<<<
The parallel sentences in question were, in their simple form, (a) The poor people applied for them to the Town Hall, & (b) The poor people were served by municipal employees.
===
The parallel sentences in question were, in their simple form, (a) *The poor people applied for them to the Town Hall, &* (b) *The poor people were served by municipal employees.*
>>>

<<<
The writer has decided, for the sake of emphasizing Town Hall, to rewrite a in the it was ... that form; but he has forgotten that he cannot make a dependent & leave b independent
===
The writer has decided, for the sake of emphasizing *Town Hall,* to rewrite *a* in the *it was . . . that* form; but he has forgotten that he cannot make *a* dependent & leave *b* independent
>>>

<<<
unless he supplies the latter with a subject (& they were served).
===
unless he supplies the latter with a subject (& *they were served*).
>>>

<<<
The correct possibilities are: (i, both independent) The people applied to the Town Hall for them, & were served by municipal employees;
===
The correct possibilities are: (i, both independent) *The people applied to the Town Hall for them, & were served by municipal employees;*
>>>

<<<
(ii, both dependent) It was to the Town Hall that the people applied, & by municipal employees that they were served;
===
(ii, both dependent) *It was to the Town Hall that the people applied, & by municipal employees that they were served;*
>>>

<<<
(iii, dependent & independent) It was to the Town Hall that the people applied, & they were served by municipal employees.
===
(iii, dependent & independent) *It was to the Town Hall that the people applied, & they were served by municipal employees.*
>>>

